@startuml
!include _style.iuml
skinparam BackgroundColor #ffffff
' scripts/aws/v1/definitions.py: queues, DLQs and event source mappings
' processing/handlers.py; processing/worker/sqs.py
 title Deployment view · four queue lanes and consumers · dc2-live
 left to right direction
 skinparam defaultFontSize 20
 skinparam ArrowFontSize 18
 skinparam titleFontSize 21
 skinparam LegendFontSize 18
 skinparam nodesep 24
 skinparam ranksep 16
 node "MediaRepair" as mr $MEDIA
 node "Processing relays\nCommands, Repair,\nEcsEvents, S3Events" as relay $PROC
 queue "ProcessingCommandsQueue\n+ DLQ" as cq $INFRA
 queue "ProcessingWorkQueue\n+ DLQ" as wq $INFRA
 queue "ProcessingShortWorkQueue\n+ DLQ" as sq $INFRA
 queue "MediaResultsQueue\n+ DLQ" as rq $INFRA
 node "ProcessingCommands\ncommand_handler" as pc $PROC
 node "Fargate worker 0..3\nReceive / Delete" as w $PROC
 node "ProcessingShortEncoder\nshort_encoder_handler" as sh $PROC
 node "MediaResults\nresult_handler" as res $MEDIA
 mr --> cq : commands
 cq --> pc : mapping\n10 / cap 2
 relay --> wq : standard
 relay --> sq : short
 relay --> rq : results
 wq --> w : polled\n(no mapping)
 sq --> sh : mapping\n1 / cap 2
 rq --> res : mapping\n10 / cap 2
 legend bottom
 Blue Media · amber Processing · slate SQS (outside the VPC).
 Arrows: send and delivery. "10 / cap 2" = batch size / concurrency.
 Each queue moves a message to its DLQ after 5 receives.
 Visibility: 420 s (short work 960 s). Encoders write SQL; relays send.
 endlegend
@enduml
